    <record id="article_code_of_conduct" model="wiki.article">
        <field name="sequence">40</field>
        <field name="name">Code of Conduct</field>
        <field name="slug">code_of_conduct</field>
        <field name="icon">shield</field>
        <field name="meta">Updated 11 Jun 2026 · People Team · v3</field>
        <field name="description">How we work, treat each other, and represent Ethara.</field>
    </record>
    <record id="article_code_of_conduct_s1" model="wiki.article.section">
        <field name="article_id" ref="article_code_of_conduct"/><field name="sequence">10</field>
        <field name="heading">Purpose</field>
        <field name="body">Our Code of Conduct sets the standard for how we work, treat each other, and represent Ethara — for every employee, contractor, and partner, on day one and every day after.

It sits alongside the POSH policy and the grievance channel. Where this Code is silent, use good judgement and ask the People Team.</field>
    </record>
    <record id="article_code_of_conduct_s2" model="wiki.article.section">
        <field name="article_id" ref="article_code_of_conduct"/><field name="sequence">20</field>
        <field name="heading">Expected conduct</field>
        <field name="body">We hold each other to a high bar. The behaviours below are non-negotiable, regardless of role, seniority, or location.

• Act with integrity — be honest, keep commitments, and never misrepresent your work or the company.
• Treat everyone with respect — no discrimination, bullying, or demeaning language.
• Protect what's confidential — handle employee and customer data on a need-to-know basis.
• Disclose conflicts of interest — outside work, gifts, and relationships that could bias a decision.
• Keep the workplace safe — follow safety guidance and report hazards promptly.</field>
    </record>
    <record id="article_code_of_conduct_s3" model="wiki.article.section">
        <field name="article_id" ref="article_code_of_conduct"/><field name="sequence">30</field>
        <field name="heading">Anti-harassment</field>
        <field name="body">Ethara has zero tolerance for harassment of any kind — including sexual harassment as defined under the POSH Act. This applies to every interaction: in the office, on calls, over chat, and at company events.

Harassment includes unwelcome conduct, comments, or advances that create an intimidating, hostile, or offensive environment. If you experience or witness it, you are encouraged — never required to be certain first — to raise a concern.

Reports are handled confidentially by the Internal Committee. Anonymous reports are supported, and retaliation against anyone who raises a good-faith concern is itself a breach of this Code.</field>
    </record>

